WARRANT FOR TARGETING (the tables' rule: re-run an earlier kill iff EVERY row it last reddened sits in a session whose
COMMAND LIST changed).  Command-changed: rearm, latch x5, gate, keeps.  Derived mechanically over tables 1-7's logs (each
mutant's LATEST measured red set): 25 kills qualify -- listed below.  The eight free-running sessions are NEW (no earlier
kill stands on them).  The Opus seat's ten close-4 mutants were measured by that seat at 131/131 on table 7's
instrument (opus_close4_20260914/table_c4*.out); they are re-run here on the NEW instrument only.  Four of the 25 were
last measured in table 3 on a SMALLER instrument (nolatch, lt_wset, rearm, static_od); their predictions below are
DERIVED for today's 141 rows, not carried, and are expected to be larger than their table-3 sets.

FOUR PROBE LANES, the earlier tables' warrant (step-counted oracles); a red row outside its prediction is re-run alone.

